---

<div class="prose-letter space-y-8">
  <div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Agreement</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
      These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your use of Harvous, a Bible study notes app
      operated by Testament Made LLC. By creating an account or using Harvous, you agree to these
      Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the service.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">The service</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
      Harvous helps you write, organize, and revisit Bible study notes. We may update, improve,
      or discontinue features from time to time. We try to keep the service available, but we do
      not guarantee uninterrupted access.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Your account</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
      You are responsible for your account credentials and for activity under your account. Keep
      your sign-in information secure and notify us if you suspect unauthorized access.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Your content</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
      You retain ownership of the notes and other content you create. You grant us a limited
      license to host, store, and display your content solely to operate Harvous — including
      syncing it across your devices, honoring share links you create, showing it to the people
      in spaces you share it with, and passing it to AI apps you connect.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Paid plans</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
      Harvous is free to use, and some features are part of a paid plan such as Harvous Plus. Current
      prices and what each plan includes are on the
      <a
        class="underline decoration-[var(--color-rule)] underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-[var(--color-ink)]"
        href="/pricing/"
      >
        pricing page
      </a>.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
      Paid plans are sold by Polar, our payment provider, as the merchant of record. That means
      Polar is the seller for your purchase: it takes the payment, charges any sales tax or VAT,
      and issues your receipts, and its own terms apply to the payment. A subscription renews
      automatically each month or year until you cancel it. You can cancel any time in Settings ›
      Plan; you keep your paid features until the end of the period you've paid for. If a
      subscription ends, your notes stay yours, and features that need the plan stop working.
    </p>
    {/* REVIEW: refund policy is not stated anywhere in the app or docs. Decide on one (or defer
         to Polar's) and add it here. Also decide whether to promise advance notice of price
         changes for existing subscribers. Church plans are bought by a staff member for the
         church; confirm they need no extra terms here. */}
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Shared spaces and churches</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
      When you add something to a shared space, the people in that space can read it. Only share
      what you have the right to share. The owner of a space decides who is in it and can remove
      people. If you set up or run a church on Harvous, you are responsible for what your church
      publishes and for inviting people into its spaces, and you agree to use what Harvous shows
      you about your congregation only to serve them.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Discover</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
      Discover is a free public catalog of study starters people give away. When you submit
      something, you confirm it is yours to share, and you give us and everyone who uses Harvous a
      free, worldwide, non-exclusive permission to show it publicly with your first name and last
      initial, and to copy it into their own Harvous accounts and use it there. We review
      submissions and may decline or remove a listing. You can withdraw your listing at any time;
      it leaves the catalog, but copies people already added remain theirs.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Connector and AI apps</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
      Connector lets you connect AI apps such as Claude or ChatGPT to your Harvous account. You
      choose which apps to connect, and you can disconnect them in Settings › Connector. A connected
      app reads your study when you ask it to, and can start a new note only if you allow it. What
      it does with what it reads, and what it tells you, is governed by that app's own terms. AI
      apps can be wrong, including about Scripture, so weigh what they say. Connector has daily
      usage limits, and we may suspend a connection that is being misused.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Acceptable use</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
      Use Harvous lawfully and respectfully. Do not upload content that is illegal, harassing,
      hateful, or that infringes someone else's rights. Do not attempt to disrupt the service,
      scrape it at scale, reverse engineer it, or access other users' private data without
      permission.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Scripture and study content</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
      Harvous is a tool for personal Bible study. It is not a substitute for church community,
      pastoral counsel, or your own judgment. Bible text and reference tools are provided for
      study convenience; translation and interpretation remain your responsibility.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Disclaimer</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
      Harvous is provided "as is" without warranties of any kind, to the fullest extent permitted
      by law. We are not liable for indirect or consequential damages arising from your use of
      the service.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Termination</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
      You may stop using Harvous at any time. We may suspend or terminate access if you violate
      these Terms or if needed to protect the service or other users.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Changes</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
      We may update these Terms from time to time. When we do, we'll tell you in the app and by
      email, and summarize what changed on the
      <a
        class="underline decoration-[var(--color-rule)] underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-[var(--color-ink)]"
        href="/legal/changes/"
      >
        What changed
      </a>
      page. The updated Terms are effective on the date shown at the top. If you don't agree with
      them, you can stop using Harvous and delete your account.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Contact</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
      Questions about these Terms? Email
      <a
        class="underline decoration-[var(--color-rule)] underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-[var(--color-ink)]"
        href="mailto:derek@harvous.com"
      >
        derek@harvous.com
      </a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
